Algo-Certify 
A certificate verification system built on the Algorand blockchain. Institutions can issue digital certificates, and anyone can verify their authenticity instantly, with no middlemen and no forgery.

Problem 
Fake certificates and degrees are a real problem. Verifying a certificate today usually means emailing the issuer and waiting days for a reply.

Solution 
Algo-Certify stores a cryptographic hash of each certificate on the Algorand blockchain. To verify a certificate, we hash the document again and compare it with the on-chain record. If they match, the certificate is genuine.

Features (Planned) 

- Issue a certificate (store its hash on Algorand)
- Verify a certificate by uploading the file or entering its ID
- Revoke a certificate if it was issued by mistake
- Simple web interface

Tech Stack 

- Blockchain: Algorand (TestNet for development)
- Smart contracts: PyTeal / AlgoKit
- SDK: py-algorand-sdk or algosdk (JavaScript)
- Frontend: React (planned)
                        
